{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_136f5959512b0b1b3b47a040f9fbe09485f16c53af82f2c84b50a6143134ed98"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states codai summarizes full project context using Tree-sitter."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1c24b8dc5bbd7045ef5daad7ecc91586c5ec125bdf6122babc2b6ee3f3b5972f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Codai can be installed globally via 'go install github.com/meysamhadeli/codai@latest'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_26ea4b8e4c96bb4befa91c80c196032521164a30da2b4dd579d2876f78b190e5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is written in Go, with a badge indicating a required Go version of at least 1.23."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4af639c9eed63220200c112e982f2dff31a53644741a2dacf1d3b05c163d2073"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README notes the project is a work in progress with new features to be added over time."},{"claim_ids":["clm_69caefed51c7f3d1bc147cad55f4725f707d3757499f11421f6b0eb0a11a6cc7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README claims codai can modify several files at once and tracks and displays token consumption for each request."},{"claim_ids":["clm_75840d18cec57e0bd8531d0ebfbeb2ee28f2bb455e782e2e9560c1c5c3fa7bc9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Users select an LLM provider with a '--provider' flag and a model with '--model'; OpenAI is stated as the default provider, with listed providers including Ollama, Azure OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Mistral, Grok, Qwen, DeepSeek, and OpenRouter."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b9100d79b6269b6ade9da5aea61367409065c0e7222473ccf49aeea67bb83e86"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Codai is described as an AI coding agent that runs in the terminal, invoked with the command 'codai code' from a working directory."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bd293867aa018a52465bad51d9e4d0fa75c9d2172e804131e37a116b6a1f152e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Advertised coding capabilities include adding features or tests, refactoring, describing and suggesting bug fixes, code review assistance, applying AI-generated changes, and generating documentation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c2cf56ce38fb284e25d0a636aa8ce7f29d12f2593321324ade2fa5bb3c73de58"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README claims context-aware code completions and per-session maintenance of conversational and code context."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e855b8712a0a9872c789a642884dd3cedfb61cea464cc4fe31f6be8cb1d6fe01"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A .codai-gitignore file in the working directory root lets users specify files codai should ignore."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f505377e1017a89616602a33dedbc65d55d62dd622f44cb9a3ed8cb202ca73eb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The config file supports provider, base_url, model, optional api_version, temperature, and reasoning_effort fields, plus a theme setting; themes come from the Chroma style gallery."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fee646cc0f110e72d051eb5fba9962812a6a6e507441b331524ca8babe6736c8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration can come from a codai-config.yml in the working directory root, from environment variables, or via CLI flags such as --config, --provider, --temperature, and --api_key; defaults apply when no config file is present."}],"claim_ids":["clm_136f5959512b0b1b3b47a040f9fbe09485f16c53af82f2c84b50a6143134ed98","clm_1c24b8dc5bbd7045ef5daad7ecc91586c5ec125bdf6122babc2b6ee3f3b5972f","clm_26ea4b8e4c96bb4befa91c80c196032521164a30da2b4dd579d2876f78b190e5","clm_4af639c9eed63220200c112e982f2dff31a53644741a2dacf1d3b05c163d2073","clm_69caefed51c7f3d1bc147cad55f4725f707d3757499f11421f6b0eb0a11a6cc7","clm_75840d18cec57e0bd8531d0ebfbeb2ee28f2bb455e782e2e9560c1c5c3fa7bc9","clm_b9100d79b6269b6ade9da5aea61367409065c0e7222473ccf49aeea67bb83e86","clm_bd293867aa018a52465bad51d9e4d0fa75c9d2172e804131e37a116b6a1f152e","clm_c2cf56ce38fb284e25d0a636aa8ce7f29d12f2593321324ade2fa5bb3c73de58","clm_e855b8712a0a9872c789a642884dd3cedfb61cea464cc4fe31f6be8cb1d6fe01","clm_f505377e1017a89616602a33dedbc65d55d62dd622f44cb9a3ed8cb202ca73eb","clm_fee646cc0f110e72d051eb5fba9962812a6a6e507441b3315